      "message": "Yifan - do you off hand btw why we need to do this? I thought we had logic to prevent this issue, but given b/247575800, I think wherever there is an issue, we should remove \"optional\" and we should keep libvintf simple. So, I am a fan of this CL.\n\nDevin - can you reach out to teams individually and let them know that if they want to specifically test for these services to exist, they need to add a test specifically for this. For audio, audio.effect, gatekeeper, and graphics.mapper, this should not be necessary, and it is a friendly FYI.\n\nThe thermal HAL is explicitly marked as non-optional here in order to increase adoption since some of the APIs are needed for some important features. If this is a prophylactic change, we should split it out, but if it\u0027s needed now, we should offer to add the requirement in vts_treble_vintf_vendor_test, and wvw@ can give you context.",
